            <ArticleTitle>Priapism in the oncology setting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE STUDY" NlmCategory="METHODS">N.L. is a 20-year-old Caucasian man with no significant medical history. He presented to the hospital with a two-day history of feeling ill with intermittent nausea, vomiting, blurred vision, and headache. He also noted slurred speech and left-upper-quadrant fullness for almost a month.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
